IMPORT prelude

-- National Productivity Fund Act 2010 (Singapore) -- what the Fund may pay for and to whom (ss 3, 4, 5), the Board's power to
-- check an applicant or grantee (s 24), the offences an applicant, grantee or anyone else can commit (ss 13, 17, 25, 26 and Third
-- Schedule paragraph 10), who else is liable with a company or partnership (s 27), composition (s 28), and the Board members'
-- disqualification, conflict-of-interest and quorum rules (First Schedule paragraphs 7, 8 and 10).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/NPFA2010.txt. The deposit says the revised edition
-- "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021"; the latest
-- amendment annotated in the text is Act 29 of 2023, with effect from 18 September 2023 (ss 3(1)(ba), 4(1)(a) and (aa), 24(1),
-- 26(c) and Second Schedule paragraphs 1, 3 and 8). The arrangement of sections at the top of the deposit is out of step with the
-- body (it lists "Public servants" and "Preservation of secrecy" without numbers); the body's numbering (s 16 public servants,
-- s 17 secrecy, ss 18-23 finance) is followed here.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0192 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl: Tier 3 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked
-- a sharper question yet. For a business or person the Act decides what kind of support the Fund can give (financing, grants,
-- scholarships -- but not loans), what the Board may demand of an applicant or grantee, and what it costs to lie to it, obstruct it
-- or copy its symbol. SCOPED to those provisions and to the member rules that govern who decides on an application.
--
-- Not encoded: the Board's incorporation, seal, functions and general powers (ss 7, 8, 10-12, Second Schedule), staff (s 14),
-- personal immunity (s 15), the public-servant deeming (s 16), bank accounts, estimates, investment, accounts, audit and reports
-- (ss 18-23 and the Third Schedule other than paragraph 10), dissolution (s 6), regulations (s 29), the First Schedule's
-- appointment, revocation, resignation and circulation-of-papers rules, and the access and seizure power of s 24(2) beyond its
-- three grounds. No regulations prescribing compoundable offences were retrieved.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `National Productivity Fund Act 2010 -- the Fund and offences`

§§ `3 -- what is paid into the Fund`

-- s 3(1): into the Fund "must be paid" (a) money appropriated from the Consolidated Fund; (b) investments and "the net income from
-- those investments"; (ba) "all moneys paid to or recovered by the Board (whether pursuant to any contract entered into, any legal
-- action taken, or otherwise) in connection with the provision of any financing, incentive or grant from the Fund" [Act 29 of 2023];
-- (c) composition sums under s 28; (d) the Board's charges and fees for services.
-- s 3(2): net income is "the amount ascertained by adding to, or deducting from, the income received from investments ... any profit
-- derived or loss sustained (as the case may be) from the realisation of those investments".
DECLARE Receipt IS ONE OF
    `money appropriated from the Consolidated Fund`
    `net income from investing the Fund`
    `a grant clawed back from a recipient`
    `a composition sum`
    `a fee for a service of the Board`

GIVEN `the receipt` IS A Receipt
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the receipt must be paid into the Fund` IF
    CONSIDER `the receipt`
    WHEN `money appropriated from the Consolidated Fund` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `net income from investing the Fund` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a grant clawed back from a recipient` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a composition sum` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a fee for a service of the Board` THEN TRUE

GIVEN `investment income` IS A NUMBER, `realised profit` IS A NUMBER, `realised loss` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the net income from investments` MEANS
    `investment income` PLUS `realised profit` MINUS `realised loss`

§§ `4, 5 -- what the Fund may pay for`

-- s 4(1): the moneys "may be withdrawn and applied for all or any of the following purposes only":
--   (a) "the provision (whether directly or through an intermediary) of financing (but not loans) or incentives (including grants and
--       scholarships) to any public authority, enterprise, educational institution or other person (whether in Singapore or elsewhere)
--       undertaking or facilitating any programme on matters relating to productivity enhancement and continuing education";
--   (aa) "the provision of grants ... to any enterprise, for the purpose of -- (i) making investments in Singapore; or (ii) carrying
--       out economic activities in Singapore, in order to develop the Singapore economy or any part thereof" [both Act 29 of 2023];
--   (b) the Board's expenses; (c) the expenses of administering, investing and managing the Fund.
-- s 4(2): "a payment must not be made out of the Fund unless the payment is authorised by the Board".
-- s 5: moneys must not be withdrawn unless charged upon the Fund or authorised under this Act.
--
-- Only (a) and (aa) reach a person or business, and they differ: (a) admits financing or any incentive, to anyone anywhere, but only
-- for a productivity or continuing-education programme; (aa) admits only GRANTS, only to an ENTERPRISE, only for investment or
-- activity IN SINGAPORE, and only to develop the Singapore economy. A loan is outside both.
DECLARE Support IS ONE OF
    `financing other than a loan`
    `a loan`
    `a grant`
    `a scholarship`
    `another incentive`

GIVEN `the support` IS A Support
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the support is financing or an incentive` IF
    CONSIDER `the support`
    WHEN `a loan` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the support` IS A Support
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the support is a grant` IF
    CONSIDER `the support`
    WHEN `a grant` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the support` IS A Support,
      `for a productivity or continuing education programme` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the recipient is an enterprise` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `for investment or economic activity in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `to develop the Singapore economy` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `authorised by the Board` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Fund may provide the support` IF
        `authorised by the Board`
    AND (    (`the support is financing or an incentive` `the support` AND `for a productivity or continuing education programme`)
         OR  (    `the support is a grant` `the support`
              AND `the recipient is an enterprise`
              AND `for investment or economic activity in Singapore`
              AND `to develop the Singapore economy`))

§§ `24 -- what the Board may demand of an applicant or grantee`

-- s 24(1): the Board or an authorised officer, employee or agent "may by written notice require any person to provide, within the
-- time specified in the notice, any information or document" for inquiring into or ascertaining (a) "the truth or correctness of any
-- statement ... made, or of any information ... given, by a person who has applied for any financing, incentive or grant from the
-- Board"; or (b) "whether any financing, incentive or grant from the Board has been properly applied by the person to whom it was
-- provided" [both Act 29 of 2023].
-- s 24(2): full and free access to lands, buildings, books and papers "for any of the purposes of this Act"; may take possession if,
-- in its opinion, (a) inspection or copying cannot reasonably be done without possession; (b) they may be interfered with or
-- destroyed; or (c) they may be required as evidence in proceedings.
-- The notice in (1) may be served on "any person" -- not only the applicant -- so long as the purpose is one of the two.
GIVEN `to check an applicant's statement` IS A BOOLEAN, `to check a grant was properly applied` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Board may require information by written notice` IF
    `to check an applicant's statement` OR `to check a grant was properly applied`

GIVEN `copying needs possession` IS A BOOLEAN, `the papers may be destroyed` IS A BOOLEAN, `the papers may be needed as evidence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Board may take possession of the papers` IF
    `copying needs possession` OR `the papers may be destroyed` OR `the papers may be needed as evidence`

§§ `13 -- the Board's symbol`

-- s 13(2): any person who uses a symbol or representation which "(a) is identical with that of the Board; or (b) so resembles the
-- Board's symbol or representation as to deceive or cause confusion, or to be likely to deceive or cause confusion" is guilty of an
-- offence: (c) "a fine not exceeding $5,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 6 months or to both"; (d) for a continuing
-- offence "a further fine not exceeding $250 for every day or part of a day during which the offence continues after conviction".
GIVEN `identical to the Board's symbol` IS A BOOLEAN, `resembles it so as to be likely to deceive or confuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `using the symbol is an offence` IF
    `identical to the Board's symbol` OR `resembles it so as to be likely to deceive or confuse`

GIVEN `days continued after conviction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for misusing the symbol` MEANS
    5000 PLUS 250 TIMES `days continued after conviction`

§§ `17 -- secrecy`

-- s 17(1): "Except for the purpose of the performance of his or her duties or the exercise of his or her functions or when lawfully
-- required to do so by any court or under the provisions of any written law", a person who is OR HAS BEEN a member, officer,
-- employee, adviser or agent of the Board, or a member of a committee of the Board, "must not disclose any information relating to
-- the affairs of the Board or of any other person" obtained in the performance of duties under the Act. (2): $2,000 or 6 months or
-- both. An applicant's business information is "information relating to the affairs of ... any other person".
GIVEN `is or was a member, officer, employee, adviser, agent or committee member` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `obtained the information in the course of duties` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `disclosed it` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `disclosed in performing duties` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `lawfully required by a court or written law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the disclosure is an offence` IF
        `is or was a member, officer, employee, adviser, agent or committee member`
    AND `obtained the information in the course of duties`
    AND `disclosed it`
    AND (NOT `disclosed in performing duties`)
    AND (NOT `lawfully required by a court or written law`)

§§ `25, 26 -- obstruction and false information`

-- s 25: any person who "hinders or obstructs the Board or any officer, employee or agent of the Board acting in the discharge of their
-- duties" -- $5,000 or 6 months or both.
-- s 26: if any person (a) "forges or counterfeits any document or certificate required by the Board"; (b) "gives any information
-- required by the Board ... KNOWING it to be false in any material particular"; or (c) "obtains any financing, incentive or grant from
-- the Fund under this Act by means of any false or misleading statement or any document that is false or misleading in any material
-- particular" [Act 29 of 2023] -- $5,000 or 6 months or both.
-- Limb (b) requires knowledge; limb (c), on its face, does not: it turns on OBTAINING support by a false or misleading statement.
-- Whether a mental element would be read into (c) is a question for the courts, not answered by the text.
GIVEN `forged a document required by the Board` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `gave information known to be materially false` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `obtained support by a false or misleading statement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a section 26 offence is committed` IF
    `forged a document required by the Board` OR `gave information known to be materially false` OR `obtained support by a false or misleading statement`

§§ `27 -- who is liable with the company or partnership`

-- s 27(1): where an offence by a body corporate is proved "(a) to have been committed with the consent or connivance of an officer; or
-- (b) to be attributable to any act or default on the officer's part", the officer as well as the body corporate is guilty.
-- (3) the same for a partner of a partnership; (5) for an officer or governing-body member of an unincorporated association.
-- (4) for a limited liability partnership: "consent or connivance of, or ... attributable to any NEGLECT on the part of, a partner or
-- manager". "Officer" (6) includes a director, chief executive officer, manager, secretary "and includes any person purporting to act
-- in any such capacity".
GIVEN `the organisation committed an offence under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `with the person's consent or connivance` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `attributable to the person's act, default or neglect` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer or partner is also guilty` IF
        `the organisation committed an offence under the Act`
    AND (`with the person's consent or connivance` OR `attributable to the person's act, default or neglect`)

§§ `28 -- composition`

-- s 28(1): an Executive Secretary or authorised officer "may compound any offence under this Act which is prescribed as a
-- compoundable offence by collecting ... a sum not exceeding the lower of the following: (a) one half of the amount of the maximum fine
-- that is prescribed for the offence; or (b) $2,000". (2) on payment no further proceedings; (4) the sums go into the Fund.
-- The base maximum fine is used; how a continuing-offence daily fine would count is not said.
GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lower of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT MOST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

GIVEN `maximum fine` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum composition sum` MEANS
    `the lower of` (`maximum fine` DIVIDED BY 2) 2000

GIVEN `prescribed as compoundable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the offence may be compounded` IF
    `prescribed as compoundable`

§§ `Third Schedule paragraph 10 -- obstructing the auditor`

-- para 10: any person who "fails, without any reasonable cause, to comply with any requirement of the auditor" under paragraph 9 (which
-- lets the auditor "require any person to provide ... any information in the possession of that person"), or who otherwise hinders,
-- obstructs or delays the auditor -- "(a) a fine not exceeding $1,000; and (b) in the case of a continuing offence, ... a further fine
-- not exceeding $250 for every day or part of a day". No imprisonment.
GIVEN `failed to comply with the auditor` IS A BOOLEAN, `had reasonable cause` IS A BOOLEAN, `hindered or delayed the auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the auditor offence is committed` IF
    (`failed to comply with the auditor` AND (NOT `had reasonable cause`)) OR `hindered or delayed the auditor`

GIVEN `days the auditor offence continued` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for obstructing the auditor` MEANS
    1000 PLUS 250 TIMES `days the auditor offence continued`

§§ `First Schedule paragraphs 7, 8, 10 -- who sits and decides`

-- para 7: a person must not be appointed or continue as a member if (a) "an undischarged bankrupt or has made any arrangement with the
-- person's creditors"; (b) "has been sentenced to imprisonment for a term exceeding 6 months and has not received a free pardon"; or
-- (c) "is incapacitated by physical or mental illness".
GIVEN `undischarged bankrupt or in an arrangement with creditors` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `months of imprisonment sentenced` IS A NUMBER,
      `received a free pardon` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `incapacitated by illness` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is disqualified from the Board` IF
        `undischarged bankrupt or in an arrangement with creditors`
    OR  (`months of imprisonment sentenced` GREATER THAN 6 AND (NOT `received a free pardon`))
    OR  `incapacitated by illness`

-- para 8(1): a member "in any way, directly or indirectly, interested in a transaction or project of the Board must disclose the nature
-- of his or her interest"; (2) must not take part in the deliberation or decision and is disregarded for the quorum; (3) no act of the
-- Board may be questioned because a member contravened the paragraph; (4) "a member whose spouse, parent, son, adopted son, daughter
-- or adopted daughter has an interest ... is deemed to be interested".
DECLARE Relative IS ONE OF
    `the member's spouse`
    `the member's parent`
    `the member's son`
    `the member's adopted son`
    `the member's daughter`
    `the member's adopted daughter`
    `the member's sibling`
    `the member's grandchild`

GIVEN `the relative` IS A Relative
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the relative's interest is deemed the member's` IF
    CONSIDER `the relative`
    WHEN `the member's sibling` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the member's grandchild` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- para 8(3): "No act or proceedings of the Board may be questioned on the ground that a member has contravened this paragraph."
GIVEN `a member failed to disclose an interest` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Board's decision can be questioned for non-disclosure` IF
    `a member failed to disclose an interest` AND FALSE

-- para 10(1): "3 members constitute a quorum and no business may be transacted unless a quorum is present"; with para 8(2)(b) an
-- interested member is disregarded for the quorum. (3) simple majority of those present and voting; the chair has a casting vote.
GIVEN `members present` IS A NUMBER, `interested members present` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Board is quorate for the decision` IF
    `members present` MINUS `interested members present` AT LEAST 3
